    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0453" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/794.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Extracts.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No revolutionary leader is as yet reported near Port au Prince. The delay in the
                    arrival of a strong presidential candidate has greatly complicated the
                    situation.</p>
                <p>Department’s instruction as to customs has been carried out. The Bank continues
                    to protest against administration of customs by revolutionists.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
